  "path": "perpendicular ray from the black hinge toward the side with more space to the grid edge",
  "trajectory": "continuous, same length as the original tail",
  "transform": "clear the original tail; keep the markers and the gray-to-black segment fixed"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-16 rows x 8-16 cols, square [observed], background=7(orange)
  colors: line=2(red), endpoint_marker=5(gray), hinge_marker=0(black)
  rods:
    count: 1-7 per grid; more rods in larger grids [observed]
    structure: straight 4-connected horizontal or vertical segment, length 3-12
    composition: one gray(5) endpoint at one end, one black(0) hinge in interior, rest red(2)
    fixed_segment: endpoint through hinge inclusive; 0-7 red pixels between them
    tail: 1-5 red pixels on the far side of hinge from endpoint
  fold_rule:
    hinge_asymmetry: perpendicular distances from hinge to opposite grid edges must be strictly unequal
    fold_direction: perpendicular to rod, toward the side with more space to grid edge
    tail_must_fit: tail length <= available space in fold direction
  placement:
    rods do not touch each other (min L1 gap >= 2 between any two rod pixels)
    folded tails must land on background cells (no collision with other rods or their fold zones)
    rods need not avoid grid edges; endpoint can be at a boundary row/col
  output:
    tail pixels erased (set to bg); same number of red pixels painted along fold direction from hinge
    markers (gray + black) unchanged; total non-bg pixel count preserved

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build folded L-shapes, then unfold tails to get straight input rods)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H=W in [8,16], choose rod count (1 for small, up to 5-7 for large).
    2. For each rod, sample orientation (H/V), fixed_segment length (2-9 incl markers), tail length (1-5).
    3. Place the folded L-shape (fixed arm + perpendicular folded arm) on the grid.
       Hinge must have strictly unequal perpendicular distances to edges; folded arm goes toward larger side.
       Ensure no overlap with previously placed L-shapes or their unfolded extents.
